.govuk-grid-row
  .govuk-grid-column-two-thirds
    h1.govuk-heading-xl.heading-with-lede Get help paying court and tribunal fees
  .article-container.group.govuk-grid-column-two-thirds
    .content-block
      .inner
        .get-started-intro
          .gem-c-govspeak.govuk-govspeak
            p.govuk-body-small You can apply for money off a #{link_to 'court or tribunal fee', 'https://www.gov.uk/court-fees-what-they-are', class: 'external', rel: 'external'}. You can do this before or after you pay the fee.
            p.govuk-body-small If you’ve already paid the fee, you can apply to get money back if both of the following apply:
            ul.govuk-list.govuk-list--bullet
              li you paid the fee in the last 3 months
              li you were eligible for help when you paid it
            p.govuk-body-small There are different rules in #{link_to 'Northern Ireland', 'https://www.justice-ni.gov.uk/articles/court-fees-0', class: 'external', rel: 'external'} and #{link_to 'in Scotland', 'http://www.scotcourts.gov.uk/taking-action/court-fees', class: 'external', rel: 'external'}.
            .govuk-details__text
              p.govuk-body-small This guide is also available #{link_to 'in Welsh (Cymraeg)', 'https://www.gov.uk/help-i-dalu-ffioedd-llysoedd-a-thribiwnlysoedd', class: 'external', rel: 'external'}.
            br
            h2.govuk-heading-m Eligibility
            p.govuk-body-small Whether you’re eligible depends on:
            ul.govuk-list.govuk-list--bullet
              li how much money you have in savings
              li which benefits you get
              li your income
            h3.govuk-heading-s Your savings
            p.govuk-body-small You must have less than the maximum amount of savings to be eligible. If you have a partner, you must include their savings too.
            p.govuk-body-small If you and your partner are 65 or younger, the maximum amount of savings you can have depends on how much the court or tribunal fee is.
            p.govuk-body-small For example, you can have:
            ul.govuk-list.govuk-list--bullet
              li up to £4,250 in savings if your fee is £1,420 or less
              li up to £16,000 in savings if your fee is over £7,000
            p.govuk-body-small Most court and tribunal fees are less than £1,420.
            p.govuk-body-small If you or your partner are 66 or older, you can have up to £16,000 in savings, whatever your fee is.
            p.govuk-body-small #{link_to 'Read further guidance', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/how-to-apply-for-help-with-a-court-or-tribunal-fee-ex160a', class: 'external', rel: 'external'} about how to check the amount of savings you can have.
            h3.govuk-heading-s Benefits you get
            p.govuk-body-small You can get money off your fee if you claim one of the following benefits:
            ul.govuk-list.govuk-list--bullet
              li income-based Jobseeker’s Allowance (JSA)
              li income-related Employment and Support Allowance (ESA)
              li Income Support
              li Universal Credit (and you earn less than £6,000 a year)
              li Pension Credit (Guarantee Credit)
            p.govuk-body-small You must also have less than the maximum amount of money in savings. This is usually up to £4,250.
            h3.govuk-heading-s Your income
            p.govuk-body-small Your income includes anything you earn before tax and any other payments you receive.
            p.govuk-body-small When you apply, you must report either:
            ul.govuk-list.govuk-list--bullet
              li your income in the last calendar month – for example, if you apply in January, you report your income in December
              li your average income over the last 3 calendar months - for example, if you apply in April, you report your average income between January, February and March
            p.govuk-body-small Report whichever income is lower.
            p.govuk-body-small You can get money off your fee if your reported income is:
            ul.govuk-list.govuk-list--bullet
              li £1,420 or less, if you’re single
              li £2,130 or less, if you have a partner
            p.govuk-body-small For each child you have, your reported income can be:
            ul.govuk-list.govuk-list--bullet
              li £425 more for children aged 0 to 13
              li £710 more for children aged 14 and over
            p.govuk-body-small For example, if you have a partner and two children aged 7 and 5, your reported income can be up to £2,980.
            p.govuk-body-small You must also have less than the maximum amount of money in savings. This is usually up to £4,250.
            .govuk-inset-text
              p.govuk-body-small If you earn more, you may be able to get some money off your fee. This depends on how much your court fee is.
            p.govuk-body-small #{link_to 'Read further guidance', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/how-to-apply-for-help-with-a-court-or-tribunal-fee-ex160a', class: 'external', rel: 'external'} about how to check your income.
            h2.govuk-heading-m How to apply
            p.govuk-body-small If you have more than one fee to pay, you must apply for help with each fee separately.
            p.govuk-body-small If you need help with fees for the Court of Protection, you cannot use this service. Fill in #{link_to 'form COP44A', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/apply-for-help-with-court-of-protection-fees-form-cop44a', class: 'external', rel: 'external'} instead and submit it with your court application.
            h3.govuk-heading-s Apply online
            p.govuk-body-small Apply for help with fees when you make your court application.
            = link_to checklist_path, role: :button, class: 'govuk-button govuk-button--start', 'data-module': "govuk-button" do
              = t('start_application')
              svg.govuk-button__start-icon xmlns= "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"  width= "17.5" height= "19" viewBox= "0 0 33 40" aria-hidden= "true" focusable= "false"
                path fill= "currentColor" d="M0 0h13l20 20-20 20H0l20-20z"
            h3.govuk-heading-s Apply by post
            p.govuk-body-small Download and complete #{link_to 'form EX160', 'https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/apply-for-help-with-court-and-tribunal-fees', class: 'external', rel: 'external'} for help with court and tribunal fees.
            p.govuk-body-small You can also request a paper copy of the form from #{link_to 'your nearest court', 'https://www.gov.uk/find-court-tribunal', class: 'external', rel: 'external'}.
            p.govuk-body-small Submit your help with fees application at the same time as your court application. Send both forms to the address on the court application.
            p.govuk-body-small If you’re applying for money off a fee you’ve already paid, send your help with fees application to the court or tribunal you paid your fee to.
            h2.govuk-heading-m If you need help applying
            h3.govuk-heading-s Get help with your application
            p.govuk-body-small Who you contact depends on which court or tribunal office you’re applying to. For example, if you’re applying for a divorce you can contact the #{link_to 'Court and Tribunal Service Centre', 'https://www.gov.uk/divorce/file-for-divorce', class: 'external', rel: 'external'} to find out about getting help to pay for your divorce application. #{link_to 'Find which court or tribunal office to contact', 'https://www.gov.uk/find-court-tribunal', class: 'external', rel: 'external'}.
            h3.govuk-heading-s Get help applying online
            p.govuk-body-small Contact We Are Group if you want to apply but do not have access to the internet or do not feel confident using it.
            .govuk-inset-text
              p.govuk-body-small
                | We Are Group
                br
                = mail_to 'support@wearegroup.com'
                br
                | Telephone: 03300 160 051
                br
                | Monday to Friday, 9am to 5pm
                br
                | Closed on bank holidays
                br
                | Text FORM to 60777 and someone will call you back
                br
                = link_to 'Find out about call charges', 'https://www.gov.uk/call-charges', class: 'external', rel: 'external'
